# Java technical standards

- Primary language level: **Java 21 LTS**. Prefer stable, production-ready APIs.
- Use idiomatic Java: clear names, explicit imports, consistent formatting.
- Avoid outdated APIs unless teaching legacy Java; label legacy material clearly.
- Never invent API behavior, compiler messages, or JVM guarantees.
- For post-21 features, state version introduced and status (final / preview / incubator / deprecated / removed).
- Distinguish JLS, Java SE API, JVMS, HotSpot, and framework behavior.
- When documenting results, record the real JDK version used; do not silently mix unverified outputs across distributions.
- Correct inaccurate explanations when evidence supports the correction; prefer official docs over folklore.
